{
  "raw": {
    "https://bentley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waltham-MA/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor--Experience-Design_R0006447": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor, Experience Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Experience Design Department at Bentley University invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor position in Experience Design, to begin 7/1/2027. Applications are welcome from candidates who will hold a Ph.D. by the start date and are seeking appointment at the assistant professor level, including early-career scholars and current assistant professors whose research and teaching align strongly with the department’s strengths in experience design (XD), user experience (UX), human-centered design, human-computer interaction (HCI), human factors, information design, and emerging technologies as they relate to human-centered design. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in XD and Human Factors in Information Design (HFID), with highest priority placed on the ability or clear potential to teach design-focused courses in interaction design, prototyping, and studio-based experience design, and additional value placed on the ability to teach practice oriented research courses. Across both design and research courses, the department values theoretical grounding in perception, cognition, behavioral science, engineering psychology, and human factors, as well as clear application to experience design practice. Strong candidates will be able to bridge research and practice, producing impactful scholarship while preparing students to address contemporary experience design and human-centered technology challenges in professional settings. We welcome qualified candidates whose paths connect academic research, professional practice, and industry experience. Bentley is committed to the teacher-scholar model where teaching, scholarship, service and community engagement are expected and valued. We seek qualified faculty who represent diverse backgrounds, interests and talents and share a commitment to high ethical standards and a willingness to embrace challenge and change.  About the Experience Design Department: The Experience Design (XD) Department is a collaborative, interdisciplinary academic home for faculty whose work connects design, human factors, user experience, human-centered technology, behavioral science, and business. The department prepares undergraduate and graduate students to design products, services, systems, interfaces, environments, and experiences that are useful, usable, responsible, and valuable for people, organizations, and society. XD at Bentley spans nearly 30 years of undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral education through the XD undergraduate degree program , the Master of Science in Human Factors in Information Design (M.S. HFID) program , and the experience design track within Bentley’s Executive Ph.D. in Business program . This portfolio of programs creates opportunities for faculty to teach across levels, mentor student research and applied projects, and contribute to the continued development of experience design within a business university environment. The department’s work also aligns with Bentley’s growing emphasis on technology, innovation, and entrepreneurship, including the reimagined Adamian Academic Center, User Experience Center, and planned spaces such as the Futures Lab and Build Lab. These initiatives create opportunities for high-visibility student engagement, immersive learning, prototyping, emerging technologies, and interdisciplinary collaboration. XD faculty connect teaching, scholarship, professional practice, and external engagement through applied courses, sponsored projects, research collaborations, consulting engagements, and partnerships with organizations across the private, public, and nonprofit sectors. The majority of HFID students are preparing for professional careers as practitioners in UX, experience design, product and service design, human factors, and related fields. Across programs, students often work with ambiguous, real-world problems and translate design methods, research insights, and stakeholder needs into actionable recommendations, prototypes, design strategies, and evidence-based design decisions. About Bentley and the Area: Bentley University, located in suburban Boston, is an AACSB and NECHE accredited institution that enrolls approximately 5,500 students at the undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels. Bentley is ranked at or near the top in several categories by US News & World Report, including Best Regional Universities North and Most Innovative Schools, with Bloomberg ranking Bentley in the top 20 undergraduate business programs. Bentley’s high graduation and retention rates and top-ranked Pulsifer Career Center reflect a commitment to student success and inclusiveness. With a strong faculty of teacher-scholars, Bentley strives to be a “Force for Good” through the integration of business with the arts and sciences, and a strong emphasis on ethics and social responsibility. Providing a stimulating academic community for faculty, staff, and students, Bentley supports its faculty as they pursue cutting-edge research and bring their expertise and real world understanding into the classroom.   Minimum Qualifications : Candidates must demonstrate: Applicants should have a Ph.D. in a field relevant to the theory and practice of experience design, or be scheduled to complete their Ph.D. by September 1, 2027. Teaching potential or experience relevant to design-focused, studio-based, and/or practice-oriented research courses in experience design. Scholarly, applied research, or practice-based research agenda connected to experience design practice. Service potential or experience appropriate to career stage. Relevant fields may include HCI, human factors, psychology, cognitive science, sociology, anthropology, computer science, engineering, design, design research, or other related fields, provided the candidate’s work has a clear connection to the theory and practice of experience design, UX, or human-centered design. For teaching and scholarship, evidence may include potential for, or a record of, effective teaching, student mentoring, scholarly publication, applied research, practice-based research, or related work appropriate to career stage. Preferred Qualifications: We do not expect candidates to meet all preferred qualifications. Strong candidates may demonstrate fit through varying combinations of teaching, research, applied collaboration, and professional engagement.   Teaching expertise or experience in one or more areas such as visual design, prototyping, interaction design, applied design studios, making, UX/HCI, human factors, design research, usability and evaluation, design strategy, product design, service design, systems design, service learning, sponsored projects, or community engaged projects. Research expertise in one or more areas such as applied HCI research, design methods research, UX research, usability and human factors studies, participatory or co-design, accessibility and inclusive design, systems design, systemic design, transition design, human-centered AI, responsible innovation, evidence-based design, design pedagogy, or professional design scholarship. Professional industry experience is valued but not required, and we welcome candidates whose paths connect industry, applied practice, and academic work. Candidates may demonstrate practice relevance through applied research collaborations, sponsored projects, consulting, community-engaged design, practitioner partnerships, translational research, evidence-based design work, or scholarship that informs experience design practice, industry-relevant problem solving, and real-world impact. We are especially interested in candidates whose teaching, scholarship, or applied projects could contribute to high-visibility student engagement work involving prototyping, making, emerging technologies, community-oriented collaborations, and campus-based innovation spaces. Ability or clear potential to contribute to the continued growth, visibility, and impact of experience design within a business university environment, including collaboration, curriculum development, graduate mentoring, external partnership, or program-building over time. Special Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, candidates should submit all five required application components by October 15, 2026; review of applications will begin shortly thereafter and continue until the position is filled: An up-to-date curriculum vitae. A Letter of Interest describing the candidate’s fit with the Experience Design Department, including relevant teaching areas, research agenda, applied or industry experience where relevant, and connections between the candidate’s work and experience design practice. A Teaching Statement describing the candidate’s approach to teaching and mentoring. A Research Statement describing the candidate’s scholarly trajectory and current and future research agenda. Names and contact information for three academic or professional references. References will not be contacted without prior notice. Candidates are expected to submit materials that accurately represent their own experience, accomplishments, teaching approach, and research agenda. If generative AI or other tools are used in preparing application materials, candidates remain responsible for the accuracy, integrity, and authenticity of the final submission. The Teaching Statement should address: (1) areas the candidate is prepared to teach or develop, especially design-focused and practice-oriented research courses; (2) evidence of teaching potential or effectiveness, which may include independent teaching, teaching assistant experience, curriculum development, applied research mentoring, studio or project based learning, industry-engaged teaching, or mentoring of professional or graduate students; and (3) prior or planned approaches to inclusive, accessible, and ethical design education. The Research Statement should address: (1) key research questions, methods, and contributions; (2) evidence of research productivity, which may include scholarly publications, work under review, conference papers, abstracts, posters, proceedings, design or research artifacts, or other research outputs; and (3) connections between the candidate’s work and experience design, UX, human-centered design, HCI, human factors, or related areas. The search committee may request additional materials at a later stage, such as selected publications, design or research artifacts, teaching materials, a portfolio, or evidence of teaching effectiveness. For additional information about this position, please email Jonathan Ericson, Associate Professor and Chair, Dept. of Experience Design, Bentley University (jericson@bentley.edu). Pay Transparency: At Bentley we offer a “ total rewards ” package designed to attract, motivate, retain, and reward our employees.  This includes competitive compensation, robust benefits, career development and opportunities, generous paid time off, workplace flexibility and a positive, engaging employee experience.  In alignment with the Massachusetts Pay Transparency Act and our commitment to equity and transparency, we’re sharing the salary grade range for this role. The grade range is based on market data and the scope of responsibilities. Final pay will depend on your experience, education, and other relevant qualifications. Salary Ranges (depending on rank, qualifications and experience): Assistant Professor: $137,819 - $168,446 If you have questions about the salary grade range or need additional information, please contact us at GA_HR_Employment@bentley.edu . Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. DIVERSITY STATEMENT Bentley University strives to create a campus community that welcomes the exchange of ideas, and fosters a culture that values differences and views them as a strength in our community. Bentley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, building strength through diversity. The University is committed to building a community of talented students, faculty and staff who reflect the diversity of global business. We strongly encourage applications from persons from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, covered veterans and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds."
    },
    "https://bentley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waltham-MA/Lecturer--Accounting_R0006410": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Department of Accounting at Bentley University invites applications for a lecturer position to begin in the Fall of 2027. We seek candidates with an ability and willingness to teach in the areas of taxation at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Experience with data analytics will be especially attractive. The Lecturer contract carries an eight-course teaching load to be completed in spring and fall in one academic year. While class sizes may vary, courses are generally capped at 35 students. Bentley University is committed to the teacher-scholar model where teaching, scholarship, service and community engagement are both expected and valued. We seek qualified faculty who represent diverse backgrounds, interests and talents and share a commitment to high ethical standards and a willingness to embrace challenge and change. The Accounting Department offers an array of courses supporting BS Accounting, MS Accounting, and MBA (Accounting concentration) degrees at Bentley University. We also support the Advanced Standing in Accounting program ( https://www.bentley.edu/academics/undergraduate-programs/advanced-standing-programs ) where some of our top students pursue the BS and MS degrees. The department actively engages with students outside the classroom through initiatives and support of student organizations including Beta Alpha Psi (BAP; https://www.bentleybap.org/ ), National Association of Black Accountants (NABA; https://bentley.campusgroups.com/naba/home/ ), Information Systems Audit Control Association (ISACA; https://bentley.campusgroups.com/ISACA/ ), and The Lab for Economics, Accounting, and Finance (LEAF; https://www.bentley.edu/centers/leaf ), to name a few examples. For more information about the Department of Accounting faculty, please see faculty profiles at https://faculty.bentley.edu/department.php?dept=Accounting . Bentley University, located in suburban Boston, is an AACSB and NECHE accredited institution that enrolls approximately 5,500 students at the undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels. Bentley is ranked at or near the top in several categories by US News & World Report, including Best Regional Universities North and Most Innovative Schools, with Bloomberg ranking Bentley in the top 20 undergraduate business programs. Bentley’s high graduation and retention rates and top-ranked Pulsifer Career Center reflects a commitment to student success and inclusiveness. With a strong faculty of teacher-scholars, Bentley strives to be a “Force for Good” through the integration of business with the arts and sciences, and a strong emphasis on ethics and social responsibility. Providing a stimulating academic community for faculty, staff, and students, Bentley supports its faculty as they pursue cutting-edge research and bring their expertise and real world understanding into the classroom. Minimum Qualifications : A master’s degree related to accounting is required. Professional designation preferred (e.g., CPA). Candidates should be dedicated to excellence in teaching and engaged in relevant and substantive professional practice at the time of hire while having sustained currency and relevancy through continued professional experience and engagement. Must be familiar with Brightspace and Zoom or have a willingness to learn. Bentley University makes training available for both platforms. Special Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, candidates must submit the following as part of the application before October 15, 2026 . A current curriculum vitae A letter of interest Teaching Statement, which should include a description of how the faculty member has demonstrated or intends to create and support an inclusive classroom environment Evidence of excellence in teaching (teaching evaluations) Pay Transparency: At Bentley we offer a “ total rewards ” package designed to attract, motivate, retain, and reward our employees.  This includes competitive compensation, robust benefits, career development and opportunities, generous paid time off, workplace flexibility and a positive, engaging employee experience.  In alignment with the Massachusetts Pay Transparency Act and our commitment to equity and transparency, we’re sharing the salary grade range for this role. The grade range is based on market data and the scope of responsibilities. Final pay will depend on your experience, education, and other relevant qualifications. Salary Ranges (depending on rank, qualifications and experience): Lecturer: $117,195 - $143,238 If you have questions about the salary grade range or need additional information, please contact us at GA_HR_Employment@bentley.edu . Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. DIVERSITY STATEMENT Bentley University strives to create a campus community that welcomes the exchange of ideas, and fosters a culture that values differences and views them as a strength in our community. Bentley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, building strength through diversity. The University is committed to building a community of talented students, faculty and staff who reflect the diversity of global business. We strongly encourage applications from persons from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, covered veterans and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds."
    },
    "https://bentley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waltham-MA/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor--Accounting_R0006408": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor, Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Department of Accounting at Bentley University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position to begin in the Fall of 2027. We seek candidates with research and/or teaching interests in all accounting areas. Experienced candidates are welcome to apply. Experience with data analytics, big data, text analysis, machine learning, and artificial intelligence will be especially attractive. Bentley is committed to the teacher-scholar model where teaching, scholarship, and service excellence are both expected and highly valued. We seek qualified faculty who represent diverse backgrounds, interests and talents and share a commitment to high ethical standards and a willingness to embrace challenge and change. The Department of Accounting offers undergraduate degrees as well as graduate degrees. A recent accounting research rankings list produced by BYU based on the last 12 years ranks Bentley University as #8 in Education and #13 in Auditing research productivity. Salary is competitive, and support is available for summer research, teaching, course development, and travel to professional meetings. Our scholarly research culture is vibrant and supportive. Bentley University, located in suburban Boston, is an AACSB and NECHE accredited institution that enrolls approximately 5,500 students at the undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels. Bentley is ranked at or near the top in several categories by US News & World Report, including Best Regional Universities North and Most Innovative Schools, with Bloomberg ranking Bentley in the top 20 undergraduate business programs. Bentley’s high graduation and retention rates and top-ranked Pulsifer  Career Center reflects a commitment to student success and inclusiveness. With a strong faculty of teacher-scholars, Bentley strives to be a “Force for Good” through the integration of business with the arts and sciences, and a strong emphasis on ethics and social responsibility. Providing a stimulating academic community for faculty, staff, and students, Bentley supports its faculty as they pursue cutting-edge research and bring their expertise and real world understanding into the classroom.   Minimum Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications: A qualified candidate must hold a doctoral degree (Ph.D./D.B.A.) in Accounting, be highly committed to excellence in teaching, and demonstrate strong potential for high-quality scholarly research and publication. Special Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, candidates must submit the following as part of the application before October 15, 2026 : A current curriculum vitae A letter of interest A Teaching Statement, which should include a description of how the candidate has demonstrated or intends to create and support an inclusive classroom environment ​ A Research Statement Evidence of excellence in teaching (teaching evaluations) Recent publications or current working papers Contact information for three references. References will be contacted once the candidate pool has been determined. For further information, please email Kerri-Ann Sanderson, Search Committee Chair, at: KSANDERSON@bentley.edu . Pay Transparency: At Bentley we offer a “ total rewards ” package designed to attract, motivate, retain, and reward our employees.  This includes competitive compensation, robust benefits, career development and opportunities, generous paid time off, workplace flexibility and a positive, engaging employee experience.  In alignment with the Massachusetts Pay Transparency Act and our commitment to equity and transparency, we’re sharing the salary grade range for this role. The grade range is based on market data and the scope of responsibilities. Final pay will depend on your experience, education, and other relevant qualifications. Salary Ranges (depending on rank, qualifications and experience): Assistant Professor: $168,171 - $227,526 If you have questions about the salary grade range or need additional information, please contact us at GA_HR_Employment@bentley.edu . Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. DIVERSITY STATEMENT Bentley University strives to create a campus community that welcomes the exchange of ideas, and fosters a culture that values differences and views them as a strength in our community. Bentley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, building strength through diversity. The University is committed to building a community of talented students, faculty and staff who reflect the diversity of global business. We strongly encourage applications from persons from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, covered veterans and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds."
    },
    "https://bentley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waltham-MA/Lecturer--History--Modern-East-Asia-with-a-focus-on-China-_R0006265": {
      "title": "Lecturer, History (Modern East Asia with a focus on China)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Bentley University History Department invites applicants for a full-time, renewable lecturer position in Modern East Asia with a focus on China. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. History has a strong undergraduate presence at Bentley, with nearly 200 minors, several dozen majors, and a newly established chapter of Phi Alpha Theta, the national history honor society. The teaching load is four classes a semester and History courses are capped at 30 students. The successful candidate will be an accomplished and committed teacher with a strong scholarly background and an active research agenda. They should be able to engage students in introductory surveys and upper-level undergraduate courses while contributing to the intellectual life of the department and the university. The candidate’s primary teaching responsibilities will be in Chinese history from approximately 1650 to the present. We also welcome candidates prepared to offer courses that place China in broader East Asian, transnational, or global contexts, including courses involving Japan or Korea. Depending on the candidate’s interests and departmental needs, occasional offerings might include contemporary world history, the Vietnam War, or other topics related to Asia. Bentley’s distinctive combination of business and the arts and sciences creates promising opportunities for a historian of East Asia. We are particularly interested in candidates who can help students understand the connections between modern East Asian history, capitalism, technology, and global trade. Candidates will have opportunities to develop courses that draw upon their own expertise while contributing to the department’s expanding curriculum. Bentley University is committed to the teacher-scholar model in which excellent teaching, active scholarship, service, and community engagement are expected and valued. We seek qualified faculty who represent diverse backgrounds, interests and talents and share a commitment to high ethical standards and a willingness to embrace challenge and change. The History Department offers undergraduates a wide and expanding array of courses. Our faculty are dedicated teacher-scholars with expertise and publications in the histories of colonial America, the U.S., modern and medieval Europe, the Middle East, South Asia, North Africa, the Caribbean, and Soviet and post-Soviet Russia. Members of the department have received awards for excellence in research and innovative teaching, and all are actively engaged in the administrative life of the university. Bentley University, located in suburban Boston, is an AACSB and NECHE accredited institution that enrolls approximately 5,500 students at the undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels. Bentley is ranked at or near the top in several categories by US News & World Report, including Best Regional Universities North and Most Innovative Schools, with Bloomberg ranking Bentley in the top 20 undergraduate business programs. Bentley’s high graduation and retention rates and top-ranked Pulsifer Career Center reflects a commitment to student success and inclusiveness. With a strong faculty of teacher-scholars, Bentley strives to be a “Force for Good” through the integration of business with the arts and sciences, and a strong emphasis on ethics and social responsibility. Providing a stimulating academic community for faculty, staff, and students, Bentley supports its faculty as they pursue cutting-edge research and bring their expertise and real world understanding into the classroom. For questions, contact Clifford Putney, Chair, Bentley University History Department.  Email: cputney@bentley.edu . Phone: 781-891-2285. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should have a Ph.D. in a relevant field of history, or be scheduled to complete their Ph.D. by September 1, 2027. Special Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, candidates must submit the following as part of the application before January 15, 2027: An up-to-date curriculum vitae A letter of interest A Teaching Statement, which should include a description of how the faculty member has demonstrated or intends to create and support an inclusive classroom environment Three letters of recommendation Confidential recommendations should not be handled by candidates but sent directly to the Department of History at Bentley University by U.S. mail or as attachments.  If recommenders are providing hard copies, please direct them to send the letters to:  Bentley University Department of History  175 Forest Street Waltham, MA 02452 ATT:  Stacen Goldman Electronic letters or dossiers should be emailed to sgoldman@bentley.edu . Pay Transparency: At Bentley we offer a “ total rewards ” package designed to attract, motivate, retain, and reward our employees.  This includes competitive compensation, robust benefits, career development and opportunities, generous paid time off, workplace flexibility and a positive, engaging employee experience.  In alignment with the Massachusetts Pay Transparency Act and our commitment to equity and transparency, we’re sharing the salary grade range for this role. The grade range is based on market data and the scope of responsibilities. Final pay will depend on your experience, education, and other relevant qualifications. Salary Ranges (depending on rank, qualifications and experience): Lecturer: $66,326 - $81,065 If you have questions about the salary grade range or need additional information, please contact us at GA_HR_Employment@bentley.edu . Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. DIVERSITY STATEMENT Bentley University strives to create a campus community that welcomes the exchange of ideas, and fosters a culture that values differences and views them as a strength in our community. Bentley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, building strength through diversity. The University is committed to building a community of talented students, faculty and staff who reflect the diversity of global business. We strongly encourage applications from persons from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, covered veterans and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds."
    },
    "https://bentley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waltham-MA/Visiting-Lecturer--Spanish-and-French_R0006241": {
      "title": "Visiting Lecturer, Spanish and French",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The department of Modern Languages (ML) at Bentley University seeks outstanding candidates for a one-semester Visiting Lecturer position in Spanish and French for Spring 2027, with possibilities of renewal. Bentley is committed to the teacher-scholar model where teaching, scholarship, service, and community engagement are expected and valued. We seek qualified faculty who represent diverse backgrounds, interests and talents and share a commitment to high ethical standards and a willingness to embrace challenge and change. In addition to a variety of language electives, the ML Department offers the Language, Culture, and Business (LCB) major, as well as language minors (Chinese, French, Italian, Spanish), and Spanish for Business. The Department actively engages with students outside the classroom through the Center for Language and International Collaboration (CLIC) . We also work closely with the Office of International Education . Bentley University, located in suburban Boston, is an AACSB and NECHE accredited institution that enrolls approximately 5,500 students at the undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels. Bentley is ranked at or near the top in several categories by US News & World Report, including Best Regional Universities North and Most Innovative Schools, with Bloomberg ranking Bentley in the top 20 undergraduate business programs. Bentley’s high graduation and retention rates and top-ranked Pulsifer Career Center reflects a commitment to student success and inclusiveness. With a strong faculty of teacher-scholars, Bentley strives to be a “Force for Good” through the integration of business with the arts and sciences, and a strong emphasis on ethics and social responsibility. Providing a stimulating academic community for faculty, staff, and students, Bentley supports its faculty as they pursue cutting-edge research and bring their expertise and real world understanding into the classroom. Job Description Summary The successful candidate must demonstrate a commitment to world language teaching, possess native or near-native fluency in Spanish and French, and hold at a minimum a master’s degree. We seek individuals committed to innovative language and culture teaching practices. Lecturers in the Modern Languages Department regularly have an assignment of four (4) courses per semester, typically teaching beginning and intermediate language courses, in addition to a service component such as course coordination, or other departmental services related to the position. We seek a candidate whose main focus is language pedagogy or a closely related field and will emphasize applying the latest methods and practices in L2 pedagogy, Heritage Learners, and SLA (such as task-based activities) to coordinate and enhance our LCB major. Criteria for selection include a) an ability to teach Spanish and French, b) proven effective teaching of both languages at all levels, especially beginning and intermediate, and c) native or near-native linguistic proficiency in both Spanish and French. Minimum Qualifications M.A. or Ph.D. in French or Spanish by the time of appointment. Candidates should possess a minimum of two years of university-level teaching experience and demonstrate a deep commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level. Candidates must be eager to work in a department with a tradition of teamwork, teaching, advising, and service. Additionally, candidates must have native or near-native proficiency in Spanish, French, and English, and be willing to teach in any of those languages. Special Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, candidates should submit the following as part of the application: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter highlighting desired qualifications for the position and specific interest in Bentley and its Modern Languages department. A Teaching Statement, which should include a description of how the candidate has demonstrated or intends to create and support an inclusive classroom environment. For additional information about this position, please contact the Chair of the Modern Languages Department Christian Rubio (crubio@bentley.edu). For best consideration, please apply by September 20. Pay Transparency: At Bentley we offer a “ total rewards ” package designed to attract, motivate, retain, and reward our employees.  This includes competitive compensation, robust benefits, career development and opportunities, generous paid time off, workplace flexibility and a positive, engaging employee experience.  In alignment with the Massachusetts Pay Transparency Act and our commitment to equity and transparency, we’re sharing the salary grade range for this role. The grade range is based on market data and the scope of responsibilities. Final pay will depend on your experience, education, and other relevant qualifications. Salary Ranges (depending on rank, qualifications and experience): Visiting Lecturer: $68,036 - $92,049 If you have questions about the salary grade range or need additional information, please contact us at GA_HR_Employment@bentley.edu . Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. DIVERSITY STATEMENT Bentley University strives to create a campus community that welcomes the exchange of ideas, and fosters a culture that values differences and views them as a strength in our community. Bentley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, building strength through diversity. The University is committed to building a community of talented students, faculty and staff who reflect the diversity of global business. We strongly encourage applications from persons from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, covered veterans and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds."
    },
    "https://bentley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waltham-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer--Spanish_R0006237": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Spanish",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary The Modern Languages Department at Bentley University is accepting applications for a part-time Adjunct Lecturer, Spanish for the Fall 2026 semester. Applicants must be available to teach between 9:00 a.m. and 1:00 p.m. Courses are scheduled Monday-Wednesday and Tuesday-Friday. Primary Responsibilities: Teach Spanish Basic and Intermediate courses Create an effective classroom environment that fosters student’s curiosities and abilities to practice their language skills. Deliver course content that meets learning outcomes and encourage student’s active participation in the classroom and beyond. Promote the study of languages, including the Language, Culture and Business major . Collaborate in the development and continued assessment of learning outcomes for use in program reviews and curriculum revision. Hold office hours. Minimum Qualifications: MA required. Native or near-native competency in Spanish is required. Have at least two years of teaching experience. Have experience using and developing a range of learning materials. Preferred Qualifications:  PhD preferred.  Work Environment: Availability required between 9:00 a.m. and 1:00 p.m. Courses meet on Monday-Wednesday and Tuesday-Friday schedules. Pay Transparency: At Bentley we offer a “ total rewards ” package designed to attract, motivate, retain, and reward our employees.  This includes competitive compensation, robust benefits, career development and opportunities, generous paid time off, workplace flexibility and a positive, engaging employee experience.  In alignment with the Massachusetts Pay Transparency Act and our commitment to equity and transparency, we’re sharing the salary grade range for this role. Salary Range: Compensation for adjunct faculty is governed by the collective bargaining agreement between Bentley University and the Service Employees International Union (SEIU) Local 509. For the 2026–27 academic year, adjunct faculty are compensated at a rate of $7,225.00 per course. Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. DIVERSITY STATEMENT Bentley University strives to create a campus community that welcomes the exchange of ideas, and fosters a culture that values differences and views them as a strength in our community. Bentley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, building strength through diversity. The University is committed to building a community of talented students, faculty and staff who reflect the diversity of global business. We strongly encourage applications from persons from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, covered veterans and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds."
    },
    "https://bentley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waltham-MA/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor--Law_R0006229-1": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor, Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Law Department at Bentley University is seeking applicants for a tenure track, full-time position at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin July 1, 2027. While class sizes may vary, Law courses are generally capped at 35 students. The department seeks to acquaint students with the legal consequences of their business decisions, as well as to help them understand the role of law in society beyond the business world. The role requires teaching our undergraduate business law class and, possibly, our graduate course in law, ethics, and social responsibility. We seek candidates who can also add to our strengths in Health Law, Securities Law, and social justice law courses. Candidates with the ability and willingness to teach in one or more of these areas are especially attractive. In addition to teaching, the chosen candidate will be expected to publish high quality and impactful scholarship in respected academic journals, engage in service to both the Department and the University, and participate fully in the Department and University communities. Applicants must also be willing to work with students outside the classroom in a variety of capacities (e.g., advising students, engaging outside speakers, advising student organizations, working with service learning and career services, or other relevant activities). The Law Department currently offers both an undergraduate Business Law Major and a Law Minor. Both the Major and Minor seek to serve a broad range of business students and are not intended as preparation for law school. Instead, they provide an in-depth study of business laws that impact specific arenas of a business enterprise, while also offering an examination of the intersection of business laws with other laws, including those that attempt to address public policy and social justice issues. The Department offers Pre-Law Advising to students interested in attending law school. We also seek to actively engage with students through our Adamian Law Club and Moot Court Team. More information about the Bentley University Law Department is available at: Bentley University Law Department Bentley is committed to the teacher-scholar model where teaching, scholarship, service and community engagement are expected and valued. We seek qualified faculty who represent diverse backgrounds, interests and talents and share a commitment to high ethical standards and a willingness to embrace challenge and change. Bentley University, located in suburban Boston, is an AACSB and NECHE accredited institution that enrolls approximately 5,500 students at the undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels. Bentley is ranked at or near the top in several categories by US News & World Report, including Best Regional Universities North and Most Innovative Schools, with Bloomberg ranking Bentley in the top 20 undergraduate business programs. Bentley’s high graduation and retention rates and top-ranked Pulsifer Career Center reflects a commitment to student success and inclusiveness. With a strong faculty of teacher-scholars, Bentley strives to be a “Force for Good” through the integration of business with the arts and sciences, and a strong emphasis on ethics and social responsibility. Providing a stimulating academic community for faculty, staff, and students, Bentley supports its faculty as they pursue cutting-edge research and bring their expertise and real world understanding into the classroom. Minimum Qualifications: Juris Doctorate (JD) Demonstrated potential for excellent undergraduate and/or graduate teaching. Promise of producing high quality and impactful scholarship. Evidence of a willingness to engage with students outside the classroom and to participate  in department and university service. Familiarity with Brightspace and Zoom or a willingness to learn. Bentley University makes training available for both platforms Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching undergraduate law courses within a business program/curriculum. Proven ability to publish in law reviews. Special Instructions to Applicants: For best consideration, please apply by October 1, 2026.  All applicants will be asked to include the following documents as part of their application: CV A letter of interest indicating why the candidate is a good fit at Bentley and its Law department. A Teaching Statement, which should include a description of how the faculty member has demonstrated or intends to create and support an inclusive classroom environment. A Research Statement, which should describe the faculty member’s plans for developing a research stream and/or area of legal expertise. Pay Transparency: At Bentley we offer a “ total rewards ” package designed to attract, motivate, retain, and reward our employees.  This includes competitive compensation, robust benefits, career development and opportunities, generous paid time off, workplace flexibility and a positive, engaging employee experience.  In alignment with the Massachusetts Pay Transparency Act and our commitment to equity and transparency, we’re sharing the salary grade range for this role. The grade range is based on market data and the scope of responsibilities. Final pay will depend on your experience, education, and other relevant qualifications. Salary Ranges (depending on rank, qualifications and experience): Assistant Professor: $111,666 - $151,078 If you have questions about the salary grade range or need additional information, please contact us at GA_HR_Employment@bentley.edu . Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. DIVERSITY STATEMENT Bentley University strives to create a campus community that welcomes the exchange of ideas, and fosters a culture that values differences and views them as a strength in our community. Bentley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, building strength through diversity. The University is committed to building a community of talented students, faculty and staff who reflect the diversity of global business. We strongly encourage applications from persons from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, covered veterans and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds."
    },
    "https://bentley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waltham-MA/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Associate-Professor--Finance_R0006218": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant/Associate Professor, Finance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Finance Department at Bentley University is seeking applications for two candidates at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor to begin in July 2027. Candidates should have a doctoral degree in finance or a related field and demonstrate excellence in teaching and scholarly research. We have a strong preference for candidates with the ability to teach courses across all areas of finance, potentially both in-person and online, at the undergraduate and graduate levels (MBA/MS programs). We have a strong preference for candidates at either rank with the ability and willingness to collaborate with colleagues and have teaching experience in Finance at both the undergraduate and graduate levels (MBA/MS programs). Familiarity with digital databases such as Bloomberg Terminal, FactSet, CapIQ, and Morningstar Direct and their use in finance courses is desirable. Associate Professor candidates should demonstrate excellence in teaching and scholarly research, with evidence of the ability to publish top-tier research to warrant appointment at the Associate Professor level, and research expertise in topics including behavioral finance, corporate finance, fixed income, investments, fintech, or asset pricing.  For more information on the department and its faculty, please see: https://www.bentley.edu/academics/departments/finance . Salary is competitive, and support is available for summer research and travel to professional meetings.  Bentley is committed to the teacher-scholar model where teaching, scholarship, service and community engagement are expected and valued.  We seek qualified faculty who represent diverse backgrounds, interests and talents and share a commitment to high ethical standards and a willingness to embrace challenge and change. Our finance faculty are actively engaged in research and have published in well-regarded journals. The Finance department encourages and values experiential learning and offers an array of courses supporting undergraduate degrees in Finance, Economics and Finance, Corporate Finance and Accounting, FinTech, Financial Planning and Wealth Management, as well as master’s degrees in Finance, FinTech, Financial Planning and Wealth Management, and MBA (Finance) degrees. The MS Finance program is ranked 44th in global Masters programs and 1st in the U.S. by the 2025 Financial Times. For more information on its graduate programs, see: https://www.bentley.edu/academics/graduate-programs/masters-finance . We also offer the Advanced Standing in Finance program ( https://www.bentley.edu/academics/undergraduate-programs/advanced-standing-programs ) where some of our top students pursue BS and MS degrees in Finance at Bentley. The department actively engages with students outside the classroom through initiatives and support of student organizations, including the Bentley Investment Group ( https://www.bentley.edu/centers/trading-room/bentley-investment-group ), the Lab for Economics, Accounting, and Finance ( https://www.bentley.edu/centers/leaf ), and the Trading Room ( https://www.bentley.edu/centers/trading-room ) to name a few examples. The Trading Room offers 24 Bloomberg terminals and subscriptions to FactSet, CapIQ, Morningstar Direct, and Financial Trading Systems (FTS). The Academic Technology Center (ATC) provides strong support for faculty research through Bentley’s subscription to a range of financial data, including IBES, ISS databases, Thompson Reuters, CRSP Mutual Fund, Trace, SDC, to name a few, in addition to standard databases such as CRSP and Compustat. Bentley University, located in suburban Boston, is an AACSB and NECHE-accredited institution that enrolls approximately 5,500 students at the undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels. Bentley is highly ranked in several categories by U.S. News & World Report for 2026, including #1 in Regional Universities North, #4 Most Value Schools (North), and #12 Overall College in the U.S. (Wall Street Journal).  Bloomberg ranks Bentley #12 in the U.S. Bentley’s high graduation and retention rates, and top-ranked Pulsifer Career Center reflect a commitment to student success and inclusiveness. With a strong faculty of teacher-scholars, Bentley strives to be a “Force for Good” through the integration of business with the arts and sciences, and a strong emphasis on ethics and social responsibility. Providing a stimulating academic community for faculty, staff, and students, Bentley supports its faculty as they pursue cutting-edge research and bring their expertise and real-world understanding into the classroom. Application materials should be submitted through Bentley's on-line employment site at: https://bentley.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/faculty Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. For full consideration, candidates must submit the following as part of the application: An up-to-date curriculum vitae. A letter of interest indicating why the candidate is a good fit at Bentley and its Finance department. A Teaching Statement, which should include a description of how the faculty member has demonstrated or intends to create and support an inclusive classroom environment. Sample(s) of research work, and a brief statement on research area and contribution Please provide contact information for three references. Pay Transparency: At Bentley we offer a “ total rewards ” package designed to attract, motivate, retain, and reward our employees.  This includes competitive compensation, robust benefits, career development and opportunities, generous paid time off, workplace flexibility and a positive, engaging employee experience.  In alignment with the Massachusetts Pay Transparency Act and our commitment to equity and transparency, we’re sharing the salary grade range for this role. The grade range is based on market data and the scope of responsibilities. Final pay will depend on your experience, education, and other relevant qualifications. Salary Ranges (depending on rank, qualifications and experience): Assistant Professor: $201,248 - $245,969 Associate Professor: $208,080 - $254,320 If you have questions about the salary grade range or need additional information, please contact us at GA_HR_Employment@bentley.edu . Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. DIVERSITY STATEMENT Bentley University strives to create a campus community that welcomes the exchange of ideas, and fosters a culture that values differences and views them as a strength in our community. Bentley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, building strength through diversity. The University is committed to building a community of talented students, faculty and staff who reflect the diversity of global business. We strongly encourage applications from persons from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, covered veterans and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds."
    },
    "https://bentley.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waltham-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer---Law--Pooled-Posting-_R0006079": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer,  Law (Pooled Posting)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary The Law Department at Bentley University is always interested in learning about qualified candidates for Law adjunct faculty positions. Openings for these positions are not always available, but we encourage all qualified applicants to put their application into this pool as openings can occur at any time. Given our current course offerings, our teaching needs most likely would be for our courses in Commercial Law, Environmental Law, Health Law, Securities Law, and Social Justice Law. Therefore, if an applicant has expertise in one of these areas, they are encouraged to list that expertise in their application and/or cover letter. It is possible that expertise in other topical areas may become of interest as we develop new courses or experience changes in our current faculty so applicants should list these as well. Based on the needs of the Department, we will actively source candidates from this applicant pool when hiring Law adjunct faculty. Pay Transparency: At Bentley we offer a “ total rewards ” package designed to attract, motivate, retain, and reward our employees.  This includes competitive compensation, robust benefits, career development and opportunities, generous paid time off, workplace flexibility and a positive, engaging employee experience.  In alignment with the Massachusetts Pay Transparency Act and our commitment to equity and transparency, we’re sharing the salary grade range for this role. Salary Range: Compensation for adjunct faculty is governed by the collective bargaining agreement between Bentley University and the Service Employees International Union (SEIU) Local 509. For the 2025–26 academic year, adjunct faculty are compensated at a rate of $7,225.00 per course. Courses with labs and other four-credit courses shall will be compensated at a higher minimum rate of $9,333.00 per course. If you have questions about the salary grade range or need additional information, please contact us at GA_HR_Employment@bentley.edu.  Bentley University requires references checks and may conduct other pre-employment screening. DIVERSITY STATEMENT Bentley University strives to create a campus community that welcomes the exchange of ideas, and fosters a culture that values differences and views them as a strength in our community. Bentley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, building strength through diversity. The University is committed to building a community of talented students, faculty and staff who reflect the diversity of global business. We strongly encourage applications from persons from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, covered veterans and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds."
    },
